      <PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>the organization is dedicated to celebrating the diverse heritage of the historically minority community of Linda Vista in San Diego, California. The organization aims to enhance the strong community spirit by partnering with local businesses and organizations to create community events and experiences.</PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>The organization successfully managed and operated the Linda Vista Certified Farmers' Market, holding 48 markets throughout 2024. The farmers' market serves as a vital space for civic engagement, access to fresh produce from local farmers, and support for unique micro-enterprises owned by residents. The market reached approximately 11,000 individuals and generated $343,650 in revenue for local vendors and farmers, demonstrating significant economic impact for the community. Vendors at the market accept EBT and participate in the Market Match program, a project of the Ecology Center funded in part by the California Department of Food and Agriculture and the USDA's National Institute of Food and Agriculture. Market Match provides a monetary incentive to customers who spend their CalFresh EBT card benefits at the farmers' market, giving them additional funds in the form of tokens or vouchers to purchase fruits and vegetables. In 2024, the organization administered $37,604 in EBT (CalFresh) transactions and distributed $34,967 in Market Match incentives, making healthy food more accessible to the community.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>103290</ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>The organization hosted multiple cultural events and community celebrations at the farmers' market throughout the year, including Lunar New Year, Mexican Independence Day, and Halloween festivities. These events celebrated the diverse Latin and Asian communities of Linda Vista, providing free activities and performances that fostered a sense of unity and cultural appreciation within the neighborhood. The market also featured live music on various occasions to enhance the community experience.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>On the fourth Thursday of every month, the organization hosted "Nonprofit Days" at the farmers' market, partnering with local nonprofits to provide a range of free services to the community, including vaccines, tuberculosis education and screenings, weekly blood pressure monitoring, senior services, and assistance with filling out paperwork for SNAP, WIC, and Medi-Cal. These collaborations helped improve access to healthcare and social services for Linda Vista residents throughout 2024.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
